# DukaanDost local settings
#
# How to fill this in
# 1. Copy this file to `.env` in the repository root (the same folder as this file).
#    PowerShell, from the repo root:
#      Copy-Item .env.example .env
# 2. The API reads that `.env` on startup. The frontend has no env file.
#    Vite already proxies /api and /health to http://127.0.0.1:8000.
# 3. Leave the values below if you only want the sample shop and template explanations.
#    Change a line only when you need that behaviour.
# 4. Use 1 or true to turn a switch on, and 0 or false to turn it off.
# 5. Do not put passwords, shop CSVs, or model weights in this file.
#    Do not commit `.env`. It is gitignored.
# 6. Restart the API after you edit `.env`. A running server keeps the old values.
#    Start it from the backend folder:
#      cd backend
#      .\.venv\Scripts\python -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000
#    Then, in another terminal:
#      cd frontend
#      npm run dev
#    Open http://localhost:5173

# Optional Postgres URI. Leave empty. The API uses the Data API keys below.
# SQLite is used only when the Supabase URL and key are also empty.
SUPABASE_DB_URL=

# Supabase project URL and keys from Project Settings → API Keys.
# The publishable key is public. The API must use the secret key.
# Leave both keys empty here. Put the real values only in `.env`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# Public Render API origin, with no trailing slash and no /health.
# Leave this empty until the blueprint is deployed and /health answers.
# Then copy that origin into the GitHub Actions secret BACKEND_URL.
# The keep-alive workflow does not read this file. If the secret is missing,
# the workflow exits without pinging.
BACKEND_URL=

# Browsers allowed to call the API. Comma-separated, no quotes.
# Keep both localhost and 127.0.0.1 because Windows may open either one.
# Add http://localhost:8080 only if you use Docker Compose.
# Remove an origin you do not use. Do not use * .
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173,http://localhost:8080

# Largest CSV upload, in bytes. 5000000 is 5 MB.
# A larger billing export can raise this. The API rejects anything bigger.
MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=5000000

# 1: the forecast request returns while the fit continues in the background.
# 0: the request waits until every product is forecast.
# Leave this at 1 for normal use. Tests force 0 so they can read the result immediately.
FORECAST_ASYNC=1

# 1: try TabPFN when the shop's Settings also prefer it.
# 0: never call TabPFN. Forecasts then use a named baseline
#    (seasonal_naive_7, Croston, or a moving average). The screen must show that name.
# With no API key, a missing fit, or a failed call, the forecast stays on a named
# baseline. That baseline is not labelled TabPFN.
TABPFN_ENABLED=1

# Prior Labs key from https://platform.priorlabs.ai/account/api-keys
# Leave this empty until you paste your own key. Do not commit a filled key.
# Render asks for the same name when you apply render.yaml.
TABPFN_API_KEY=

# Model name sent with the hosted prediction. v2 is the setting this app ships.
TABPFN_MODEL_VERSION=v2

# Gemma explanations. This replaces a local Ollama server.
# The API calls the OpenAI-compatible chat endpoint at LLM_BASE_URL.
# Paste a Google AI Studio key into LLM_API_KEY. Leave it empty to keep the
# English or Hinglish template. The template is also used when the call fails,
# the reply changes a number, or a limit below is hit.
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# Do not commit a filled key. `.env` is gitignored. `.env.example` stays empty.
LLM_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
LLM_MODEL=gemma-4-26b-a4b-it
LLM_API_KEY=
LLM_TIMEOUT=240
# Free tiers are rate limited: calls per minute (0 = no limit) and max seconds to wait on a 429.
LLM_MAX_RPM=10
LLM_MAX_WAIT=45
# Gemma 4 on Google: minimal thinking answers in seconds instead of minutes. Empty = provider default.
LLM_THINKING_LEVEL=minimal
# Quota guards for a public demo: model calls per day, and quota-spending requests per visitor per 10 minutes.
LLM_MAX_PER_DAY=300
SUBMIT_LIMIT=8

# Billing file opened by "open the sample shop". It is fictional.
# Leave this commented. The API then uses <repo>/samples/kirana_billing.csv.
# Uncomment only to point at a different labelled sample.
# The path is relative to the folder where you start uvicorn (usually backend),
# so the shipped sample is one directory up:
# SAMPLE_CSV=../samples/kirana_billing.csv
# Your own shop is a separate workspace. Do not point this at real sales
# if you still want the sample to stay fictional.
